From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: automation identifiers, TextBox/ScrollViewer/FocusManager members React Native asks for

OneDrive's sign-in page (React Native for Windows) stopped at each missing piece before it showed. Added: AutomationProperties' attached LiveSetting, LabeledBy, IsRequiredForForm, AccessKey, AcceleratorKey, ItemStatus and ItemType; AutomationElementIdentifiers and the 21 patterns' identifier classes (an AutomationProperty each, always the same one; ScrollPatternIdentifiers.NoScroll); FrameworkElementAutomationPeer's statics (no peer is made); TextBox's statics 2 to 8; ScrollViewer 2 to 4 (headers and settings kept, ChangeView taken, events accepted: it does not scroll yet); FocusManager 3 to 6 (TryFocusAsync and TryMoveFocusAsync done at once with their result, the static focus events accepted). AutomationProperties' string members no longer pass an unregistered property on first use.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in
index 3d98846..09ec3cb 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	binding.c \
 	application.c \
 	automation.c \
+	automation_ids.c \
 	bindinghelper.c \
 	buttons.c \
 	classes.idl \
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/automation_ids.c b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/automation_ids.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a29407d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/automation_ids.c
@@ -0,0 +1,661 @@
